1
00:00:07,510 --> 00:00:15,130
B1 David, Nora and Millie are talking about some of the world's greatest ecosystems.

2
00:00:15,130 --> 00:00:17,590
Listen to their conversation.

3
00:00:17,590 --> 00:00:23,390
Write a T if a sentence is true, or an F if it is false.

4
00:00:23,390 --> 00:00:26,775
Then correct the false ones.

5
00:00:26,775 --> 00:00:35,080
Hey David and Millie, do you know any of the biggest ecosystems on Earth?

6
00:00:35,080 --> 00:00:40,320
Yes, I know about the Amazon rainforest.

7
00:00:40,320 --> 00:00:44,350
It's the largest rainforest in the world.

8
00:00:44,350 --> 00:00:49,650
It covers around 6 million square kilometers.

9
00:00:49,650 --> 00:00:52,690
Yes, it's huge!

10
00:00:52,690 --> 00:01:02,100
It's a very important ecosystem of our planet with so many different types of wildlife.

11
00:01:02,100 --> 00:01:05,810
There's also the Sahara Desert.

12
00:01:05,810 --> 00:01:09,800
It's the largest hot desert in the world.

13
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:13,450
It covers most of Northern Africa.

14
00:01:13,450 --> 00:01:16,670
That's such a big area!

15
00:01:16,670 --> 00:01:21,340
Now, what about the ocean ecosystem?

16
00:01:21,340 --> 00:01:25,950
I know the Great Barrier Reef in Australia.

17
00:01:25,950 --> 00:01:30,580
It's the biggest coral reef system anywhere.

18
00:01:30,580 --> 00:01:38,400
By the way, did you know that Lake Baikal is the deepest lake in the world?

19
00:01:38,400 --> 00:01:41,150
No, where is it?

20
00:01:41,150 --> 00:01:43,000
It's in Russia.

21
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:45,580
I'd love to see it someday.
